  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_5428a1c1893f45e181ae5b6e033832da",
      "statement": "crates/logic (celld-logic) is celld's pure decision core with no dependencies, async, I/O, clocks, randomness, or locks; crates/celld is only an effect executor and adapter host, and no adapter may mutate core State directly.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://Cargo.toml#L1-L2",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:37e5549e11581997134f50a261bd592d07d9cab16474fbcecaa213c4f9e06735:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/lib.rs#L1-L10",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c686ab6c7c301f2a08badbf73f4f5a621d4382aa2a78baf4fba739d7eb4d7f26:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_ea104940a8b04ac18dbdb6058ec8ccb7",
      "statement": "on_event(&mut State, Event) -> Vec<Effect> is the only way behavioral state advances; Event is the only input and Effect the only output, and event-carried clock samples are folded into State with max so the core never reads a clock itself.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/lib.rs#L5215-L5223",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d5ca26c5c6ce4963490ba828d7b91e0c04d963a9a2457b3a9a2f6ae5b5d1843b:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_5e1472ee8fae4903a3c115829239e39a",
      "statement": "In production the serial Actor in crates/celld/actor.rs is the only caller of celld_logic::on_event; adapter futures never borrow core state and send versioned completion events back through its mailbox.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/actor.rs#L1-L10",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6f3bf4836204621d82c7743e123070de67298ee57442e55275663d282fa9d0cb:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/actor.rs#L3900-L3910",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:908dbfe2700a06f430f8177804a50d9879534659bdd26afa87dcc0e51ed69570:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_ff4430cf634849f792a039b6bbd8d2fb",
      "statement": "Every asynchronous effect is versioned by an OpId and completion events with an obsolete op are ignored; deterministic timers are versioned effects keyed by generation, so a stale firing from a replaced lease generation is harmless.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/types.rs#L286-L314",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:48ad4c4cf96faafc57061e11697edffe3198ab240d499d16187d6d5a1279c9f4:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/types.rs#L737-L740",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a6bee01524323d2aa85b6efbe4f926ebf0783cd404268cd7d973f52a5a09b0f5:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_0c02c25f3b614515bd0945dd4bbae1f5",
      "statement": "The Channel enum enumerates every route by which cell state leaves the process and is deliberately not #[non_exhaustive], so a new channel breaks every exhaustive shell match until its hold and release rules are decided; alarm settlement is excluded because it is replayed into the core rather than released.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/types.rs#L316-L333",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5d4c3d9064912aea231e839db85256fe576364578db387ab4d61bce1983d6f96:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_20a3e441b9c64c5aa6918ae21ee2a88a",
      "statement": "State holds the output gate as a barrier table; an open gate makes its cell active so it cannot be evicted underneath it, and a fence drains barriers to failed responses so a write is never acknowledged after the node loses authority.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/lib.rs#L487-L523",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:cea9cb3ae839002460f66b227a9c6762751ed2296aa0bec91e395c9dc84d06f9:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_1d6a82493ce94bc192199b2cd946e7d7",
      "statement": "Cold-route admission is explicit core state (activation and eviction permit sets plus a FIFO capacity-waiter queue), so a waiter with k waiters ahead is admitted within k releases and no arrival pattern can starve it.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/lib.rs#L530-L546",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:05183c9ef8b0373e62498e09588d221ef8454093bcde74e4c9976d6a70bc32aa:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_a8523bb36e1c43ffb1ed3beff46065f6",
      "statement": "Config carries the numeric policy the core enforces: max_resident, max_activations, max_evictions, max_releases, the per-cell outbound WebSocket budget, eviction ownership mode, peer protocol version, operation deadline, alarm residency window, idle eviction, and the pressure config.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/types.rs#L62-L136",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:355ca682da5e8d937a67adbadd140ced2940b88d7cf1f784757af77ca4850b7d:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_f3a2f4591e034faabc48c5f571a7e774",
      "statement": "Each cell advances through a Phase state machine from Inactive through cold-activation phases to Resident and Cleaning; celld terminology evicts a cell out of memory to Dormant, and shedding is what publishes it unowned.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/lib.rs#L100-L135",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3f4d3371118fd855efaa6a5f279cdecc0906388dcf38f5fe7091322df66f10a4:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_59ff273f670d4ec1ad1518a5c9af1fae",
      "statement": "StopCause separates exit semantics: idle eviction keeps the ownership record for a same-node rename, rebalancing eviction releases it, Reset follows a failed durability proof, and Swap moves a cell to a new generation at the same epoch with no ownership or replication change.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/types.rs#L929-L953",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:80f6bbe035a5cc97a8808ee66219f5643746bbe2a8c62685f23be90ade699fb8:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_6173c5b579914ad9a8d56bd849965c62",
      "statement": "Peer dispatch retries are allowed only when the connection was never established; every later failure leaves the outcome ambiguous, so re-sending would break at-most-once execution.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/routing.rs#L1-L13",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:adca2026b62c32ab97888505c2a82f202c20d19268ebb6e1536233d4c8673fa2:"
        }
