    {
      "id": "claim_69a861a4336642c596ae0876e46e0ae6",
      "statement": "Pressure shedding is a pure classifier of a memory sample plus the hysteresis latch and deliberately excludes residency (enforced as a hard cap at admission), while local snapshot-cache eviction is bounded by plain LRU because the cache is pure optimization.",
